{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1517587-what-is-your-favourite-discipline-of-all-time","id":1517587,"title":"What is your favourite Discipline of all time?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-07-09T12:53:15-07:00","id":1517587,"title":"What is your favourite Discipline of all time?","content":"Just out mild curiosity and my personal favourite is the Presence discipline for it\u2019s subtle uses in making people like you and encourage them to help seemingly out of free will and not being the wiser.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-09T13:36:47-07:00","id":1517590,"title":"","content":"Necromancy/Mortis, it has the fun of Thaumaturgy but is more focused and less.....excessive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-09T14:23:16-07:00","id":1517598,"title":"","content":"Temporis is my favorite all time discipline...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-09T16:24:09-07:00","id":1517604,"title":"","content":"For me I would have to say Dominate is my favorite discipline with a close second being Auspex.<br /> <br /> Dominate has a fairly unique combination of benefits:<br /> 1. Doesn't cost blood to use<br /> 2. The rank 4 &amp; 5 powers can be skipped without hurting functionality (Obfuscate 3 is easier to detect than Obfuscate 5)<br /> 3. By not having to invest in the upper two ranks, it is very XP efficient for character builds (magic paths require maxing out to learn other paths)<br /> 4. It assists in Hunting<br /> 5. It assists in Backgrounds acquisition (Herd, Resources, Domain, Allies, Retainers, etc.)<br /> 6. It assists in protecting the Masquerade<br /> 7. It can be used in Combat<br /> 8. It can be used to avoid Combat<br /> 9. Its restrictions are Eye Contact and Generation, the latter of which is countered by taking Generation at character creation.<br /> 10. The eye contact issue means you are either dealing with a blind person or are interacting with them over a video call, either way you are relatively safe.<br /> 11. Unlike the Presence discipline, there is no equivalent rite to &quot;Pavis of Foul Presence&quot; for Dominate<br /> 12. If you do go to rank 5 in Dominate, then you can enjoy daylight, food, sex, and use other people's bodies to further your goals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-09T16:56:48-07:00","id":1517608,"title":"","content":"I go with obfuscate, you can be so much creative sometimes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-09T17:00:41-07:00","id":1517609,"title":"","content":"My next favourite Discipline is Obfuscate as a great way to get out of trouble, alter your appearance, sow discord and if your skillful enough you can make a person be forgotten by even his or her loved ones. Yes I\u2019m a big fan of the less flashy powers with the exception of Protean as a close third.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-09T17:02:13-07:00","id":1517610,"title":"","content":"Obtenebration is made of twisted black joy. It's got flair, it's got mystery and it looks downright spectacular in use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-09T18:21:30-07:00","id":1517615,"title":"","content":"Visccitude.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-09T18:29:36-07:00","id":1517616,"title":"","content":"I'm with Thoth-Dominate. Starting player puts his 3 points into it and good to go, it's so front loaded and versatile. Basically interactions with humans become trivial.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-09T19:22:56-07:00","id":1517620,"title":"","content":"Celerity, Fortitude and Potence, have their charms, but, Protean, stands out for me. Though, as a player, I never really liked playing vampires; but as a Storyteller, I love running them. My knowledge of disciplines are mostly how their use fits in the story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-09T22:41:43-07:00","id":1517627,"title":"","content":"Old school <b>Mytherceria </b>(from the 1992 Players Guide to the Sabbat) with <b>Darkling Trickery, Goblinism, Earth Sword </b>and<b> Basilisk's Touch</b><br /> And Obeah/Valeren ^^^\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-10T02:12:12-07:00","id":1517633,"title":"","content":"Hard tie between Thaumaturgy (blood sorcery in general) and Vicissitude, mostly for the fun of being creative with them.<br /> <br /> In terms of practicality, the Dominate-Malkavian spread is hard to top, imo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-10T02:33:28-07:00","id":1517634,"title":"","content":"For me it is Auspex and Presence as my favourite Disciplines. <br /> <br /> Presence for the Discipline's splendid and unique focus and usefulness. Also this Discipline's Powers are definitely a distinct and honest exploration and portrayal of concepts, abilities, and ideas related to charisma, love, lust, emotions, and desire.<br /> <br /> Auspex I consider to be interesting, nice, and important as a Discipline because it is a definite portrayal of ideas, capabilities, methods, and powers related simply and directly to sight, awareness, cmmonucation, comprehension, focus, and understanding. The Powers of this Discipline are also varied and efficient, and this does definitely seem very appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-10T06:50:31-07:00","id":1517642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1517587-what-is-your-favourite-discipline-of-all-time?p=1517627#post1517627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Old school <b>Mytherceria </b>(from the 1992 Players Guide to the Sabbat) with <b>Darkling Trickery, Goblinism, Earth Sword </b>and<b> Basilisk's Touch</b><br /> And Obeah/Valeren ^^^\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Copy past to us those ppwers please","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-10T07:06:54-07:00","id":1517643,"title":"","content":"Thaumathurgy, mainly the spirit based ones. Its pretty expensive, and not really useful at times because of the relationship between vampires and spirits, but I like it mainly for the feeling of playing a spiritmancer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-10T07:47:13-07:00","id":1517645,"title":"","content":"Potence and to a lesser extent Celerity (not so much the blood burning extra actions, but the extra Dexterity dice which the people I\u2019ve played with always let add to speed calculation formulas).<br /> <br /> Vampires exist in a physical world, so being able to more easily exert yourself and move about within it is exceptionally useful in many situations. Nothing beats being able to rip a steel door off its hinges in an action or clear a 40\u2019 gap when you need to get to or away from someplace. More subtle uses like breaking ordinary locks, hopping fences in a hurry, overpowering a tough, etc. can come up enough to be valuable.<br /> <br /> Best of all, you rarely need actually spend blood for them. Three extra Dex dice is usually enough to make split dice pools for actions viable against your usual mooks. It also lets you be very stealthy (not exactly obfuscate, but still very handy and DOES work against cameras/video). Jump checks are difficulty 3 so little need to spend blood on potence for guarenteed successes.<br /> <br /> For a vampire looking to be efficient in their blood expenditure (while still having the option to burn it in an emergency), Potence and Celerity are hard to top\u2026 even if you\u2019re not looking for a fight.<br /> <br /> Honorable mentions go to Fortitude (the less damage you take the less blood you need to spend on healing) and Dominate (social manipulation that doesn\u2019t require blood expenditure).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-10T07:53:46-07:00","id":1517646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1517587-what-is-your-favourite-discipline-of-all-time?p=1517642#post1517642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Copy past to us those ppwers please</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2022 <b>Fey Sight</b><br /> A vampire with this power is in tune with faeries and things faerie. The vampire can see faerie regions (areas which are part of this world and Arcadia). They can also see through faerie glamour and see invisible faeries. The vampire can make out the faint outlines of spirits that are not on the physical plane, though this requires intense concentration.<br /> <b>System:</b> This power usually requires no special roll unless the character is trying to see a particular spirit, in which case she must roll Perception + Occult (difficult 9).<br /> <br /> \u2022\u200b\u2022\u200b <b>Darkling Trickery</b><br /> The Kiasyd can cause minor magical pranks. The vampire can create numerous spontaneous effects, and while none of them should be overtly harmful, they most certainly should be annoying to the victim. It is up to the player and Storyteller to come up with the pranks' effects.<br /> <b>System: </b>Using this power requires a Manipulation + Occult roll (difficult 7). The number of successes usually determines how long the trickery lasts.This varies based on what the trick is.<br /> Here are just a few possibilities: remove hair (the victim's hair falls out), banshee's wail (the vampire lets out a scream, deafening all nearby for an hour and causing fear in animals), blight crops (causes all plants within a 100-yard radius to wither away and die), falling stones (telekinetically causes small stones to fall), slip (causes one victim to slip on the floor unless he makes a Dexterity + Dodge roll with a difficult of 7), and foul simple machines (the vampire causes a simple machine to malfunction when the victim uses it).<br /> <br /> \u2022\u200b\u2022\u200b\u2022\u200b <b>Goblinism</b><br /> The Kiasyd has an innate understanding of earth and stone. The Kiasyd can instantly identify metals, rock formations and stones. Underground, the vampire has an intuitive direction sense. Through long and strenuous effort, the Kiasyd can also alter earth and stone. The vampire can use this power for many purposes, such as shaping tunnels, building supports for underground havens, and smoothing out surfaces into flat floors and walls.<br /> <b>System: </b>The knowledge and direction sense associated with this power do not require a roll, but shaping rock means the vampire must summon faerie goblins to aid him. The goblins will be inclined to help him, but not obligated. One goblin will appear per success on a Charisma + Leadership roll (difficult based on how far underground the vampire is -in a mine shaft would mean a difficult of 6, on the street would have a difficult of 8, and at the top of the Sears Tower would have a difficulty of 10, if the Storyteller permits it at all.).<br /> <br /> \u2022\u200b\u2022\u200b\u2022\u200b\u2022\u200b <b>Faerie Wards </b>(Same as the later edition's Chanjelin Ward)<br /> The Kiasyd can protect designated areas with faerie glyphs, causing anyone who enters the area to become extremely disoriented. Kiasyd will occasionally put these glyphs on people who have offended them, causing the victim to be disoriented until the glyphs fade.<br /> <b>System:</b> The warder must roll Dexterity + Security (difficulty 7 for inanimate objects or the target's Willpower + 2). Success means the glyphs appear wherever the warder wants and can be seen with the unaided eye. Anyone entering the protected area finds all rolls involving Mental Attributes have their difficulties increased by one. They will also become lost unless they can make an Intelligence + Investigation roll (difficulty 8). The glyphs lasts for a length of time based on the number of successes rolled. 1 Success One Hour 2 Successes One Night 3 Successes One Week 4 Successes One Month 5 Successes One Year<br /> <br /> \u2022\u200b\u2022\u200b\u2022\u200b\u2022\u200b\u2022\u200b <b>Riddle Phantastique </b>(<i>Similar </i>as the later edition's Riddle Phantastique\u200b)<br /> As soon as someone hears the Riddle Phantastique, she can do nothing but try to solve it. The Riddle is so impenetrable that it can actually damage the fragile brains of those who think about it. Malkavians and other twisted degenerates, however, seem to have an easier time figuring it out.<br /> <b>System: </b>The riddler rolls Manipulation + Faerie Lore (difficult of the victim's Willpower). After a successful roll, the victim can do nothing but sit and ponder the riddle until she accumulates five times the riddler's successes. She rolls Wits + Faerie Lore (difficult 10 minus the number of Derangements the victim has). She makes this roll as soon as she is told the riddle and then once per hour until she has gathered enough successes. Every time the victim has more botches than successes, she takes one level of damage and loses that number of successes from the accumulated total. This damage cannot be healed until the riddle has been solved. The riddler can end this trance just by telling the victim the answer, but no one else can do so.<br /> <br /> \u2022\u200b\u2022\u200b\u2022\u200b\u2022\u200b\u2022\u200b \u2022\u200b <b>Stone Travel</b><br /> The Kiasyd can travel into the earth by creating a small tunnel. The tunnels can be used by others, but they will not be very safe and they collapse easily. The vampire is able to travel underground with almost no chance of being captured.<br /> <b>System: </b>Tunneling requires physical contact with the ground as well as a Strength + Athletics roll (difficulty 6). The number of successes translates into the miles per hour at which the traveler can move. Also, the tunneler can cave in any part of the tunnel.<br /> <br /> \u2022\u200b\u2022\u200b\u2022\u200b\u2022\u200b\u2022\u200b \u2022\u200b\u2022\u200b <b>Earth Sword</b><br /> The Kiasyd cause huge, strong spikes to shoot out of walls, ceilings and floors. These will be made of whatever material they shoot out of and can be especially dangerous to vampires in wooden houses.<br /> <b>System:</b> The attacker rolls Wits + Melee (difficult 6) and spends a point of Willpower while the target resists with a Wits + Dodge roll (also difficult 6). If the attacker rolls more successes, the target takes three damage dice for each success, though the damage can be soaked normally. If the target rolls more successes, then he is unscathed. Five successes are required to impale a specific location, like the heart.<br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022\u200b\u2022\u200b\u2022\u200b <b>Basilisk's Touch</b><br /> The Kiasyd can turn victims to solid stone simply by touching them. The effects are permanent, and the only way to reverse the effect is through powerful Thaumaturgy or by another touch of the Kiasyd.<br /> <b>System: </b>This power takes effect as soon as the attacker succeeds in touching the victim and spending two points of Willpower. The victim resists with at least three successes on a Willpower roll (difficulty 8).\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-10T12:59:25-07:00","id":1517654,"title":"","content":"Vicissitude.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28074-doktor-von-zwitter","name":"Doktor von Zwitter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28074_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-10T14:50:08-07:00","id":1517658,"title":"","content":"First place is a tie between Necromancy (the Ash Path only just pulling ahead of Corpse in the Monster) and Vicissitude.<br /> Though I'm also fond of the physical disciplines; particularly Fortitude.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-10T14:58:44-07:00","id":1517660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Doktor von Zwitter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1517587-what-is-your-favourite-discipline-of-all-time?p=1517654#post1517654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vicissitude.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why exactly?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-10T16:03:37-07:00","id":1517661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1517587-what-is-your-favourite-discipline-of-all-time?p=1517660#post1517660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why exactly?</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the transformative fleshcrafting. Very transhumanist which I'm into.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28074-doktor-von-zwitter","name":"Doktor von Zwitter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28074_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-10T20:26:19-07:00","id":1517673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1517587-what-is-your-favourite-discipline-of-all-time?p=1517645#post1517645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Potence and to a lesser extent Celerity <br /> <br /> (...)<br /> <br /> For a vampire looking to be efficient in their blood expenditure (while still having the option to burn it in an emergency), Potence and Celerity are hard to top\u2026 even if you\u2019re not looking for a fight.<br /> <br /> Honorable mentions go to Fortitude (the less damage you take the less blood you need to spend on healing)</div> </div> </div> </div>At least one of the three Physical Disciplines ( or Invocations, or Powers ) is given to most Vampire Bloodlines and Kindred Clans. This notion and tendency is certainly curious, interesting, and characterful.<br /> Certainly this tendency does directly support the themes, notions, events, and choices related to survival, safety, overcoming physical ostacles, and suceeding in regard to temporal challenges. <br /> <br /> For practically all of Vampire Clans the particular Physical Discipline ( Celerity, Potence, Fortitude ) plays an interesting, curious, good, and important role in ideas and cultures of Kindred Lineages, Vampiric Sects ( the Camarilla, the Tal'Mahe'Ra, the Sabbat ) ,and also of course Kindred Clans<br /> <br /> The Physical Disciplines are useful and reliable. During many events and situations, and used in many tactics, plans, and schemes, Physical Disciplines can definitely easily and clearly change the possible outcomes and results.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-11T19:41:09-07:00","id":1517732,"title":"","content":"Also, Thaumaturgy from the Vampires Player's Guide is hard to beat. Turning someone's blood to water or making them a paraplegic is nothing to scoff at. But, may all time favorite discipline, isn't a discipline at all but a Hekau-Path: Celestial: Weather-Magic at level five. A starting level mummy can literally destroy a nation by altering its weather. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1517587-what-is-your-favourite-discipline-of-all-time?p=1517645#post1517645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Potence and to a lesser extent Celerity (not so much the blood burning extra actions, but the extra Dexterity dice which the people I\u2019ve played with always let add to speed calculation formulas). . . Fortitude (the less damage you take the less blood you need to spend on healing) and Dominate (social manipulation that doesn\u2019t require blood expenditure).</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of early V:tM players would only see there value in combat, went, Potence and Celerity have a lot of uses for a vampire from helping them hunt more efficiently to spying and gathering information. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-12T08:42:53-07:00","id":1517783,"title":"","content":"Now the physical discipline that I focus on the most is Fortitude as it's the most useful of the physical powers of being able endure considerable punishment is more important to me then being able to hit hard or move fast. Though I do try to keep at least two dots in Potence and Celerity as my characters get more experienced in there way of &quot;life&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-12T08:44:37-07:00","id":1517785,"title":"","content":"At Iguazu I was the opposite at the early days of playing games where being able gather information and spying was more useful then straight up combat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-12T10:28:41-07:00","id":1517793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1517587-what-is-your-favourite-discipline-of-all-time?p=1517785#post1517785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At Iguazu I was the opposite at the early days of playing games where being able gather information and spying was more useful then straight up combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have traumatized whole gamer groups with an opponent that was nothing more than a Tremere with Dominate 3 &amp; Path of Technomancy 5. How do you punch someone who is never there, but their influence is everywhere? Being able to hack people and computers makes for quite the power dynamic shift in the local community.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-12T11:50:32-07:00","id":1517799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1517587-what-is-your-favourite-discipline-of-all-time?p=1517793#post1517793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Path of Technomancy 5</div> </div> </div> </div>The path suffers a bit from the 90s perspective on technology and sadly wasn't updated for V20 to reflect the importance of software and data. We house-ruled the level 1 power to also apply to data analysis and the level 3 power to data manipulation in general.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-12T12:16:56-07:00","id":1517805,"title":"","content":"I love the idea of Temporis the most, messing with time as an immortal creature appeals to me but in play I really enjoy more &quot;do something right now&quot; disciplines like obtenebration, vicissitude and especially Spiritus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-12T18:53:28-07:00","id":1517853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1517587-what-is-your-favourite-discipline-of-all-time?p=1517799#post1517799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The path suffers a bit from the 90s perspective on technology and sadly wasn't updated for V20 to reflect the importance of software and data. We house-ruled the level 1 power to also apply to data analysis and the level 3 power to data manipulation in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest the Path of Technomancy suffered from the fact that WW didn't understand hacking as a non-magical process even in the 90s context. On the other hand, my group had an IRL computer security specialist, so we used that for a baseline and then upgraded the path limitations accordingly. Though that did mess with the concept that the Nosferatu were somehow the premiere hackers of the vampire community when the Tremere could just magi-hack their databases.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-13T23:53:50-07:00","id":1517923,"title":"","content":"VDA20 Serpentis is hands down my favourite. Nearly OP unless you consider that every power beyond the 1st is a likely or certain Masquerade breach. \u0130n the last session we played a few days ago \u0130 had to fight an Ahroun (the warrior auspice) werewolf on my own and \u0130 took him down in 1 turn with Serpentis 4 and Potence 4 (\u0130 play a Warrior of Glycon, the fighting Setite). \u0130 am 7th generation though and did have time and blood to meet him in peak condition. He had the first attack but the ST was also a bit unlucky with the dice. His first attack missed, my first attack was a hold with tail (from Serpentis 4) and Potence for a total of 7 successes, he did 2 Rage actions - a gift to make me fall and an attempt to break my hold - but neither worked, and then \u0130 bit him and drained him to death. Was my first fight with a Garou ever as a player, so \u0130 didn't expect it to go so smoothly. \u0130 was lucky, no doubt.<br /> <br /> After Dark Ages Serpentis, \u0130 like Potence and the physical disciplines, Dominate 1-3, Animalism 1-2 and the whole of Presence and Auspex, not necessarily in this order.<br /> <br /> With Thaum and Necro \u0130 like them some times and get bored some times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-14T01:15:16-07:00","id":1517927,"title":"","content":"For me the physical disciplines particularly fortitude, the ability to Soak Aggravated Damage is huge.<br /> <br /> Dominate is an old favourite it\u2019s caught my players out many many times.<br /> <br /> Vicissitude is my standout, it adds a Brian Lumley Necroscope quality to the fiends as being completely inhuman and can just be horrifying, even my werewolf players feared it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-14T09:05:39-07:00","id":1517954,"title":"","content":"I would give Animalism as an honorable mention as the discipline can be quite useful in many situations such as calming down guard dogs or easing the fears of most animals that encounter one of the undead and can help control your own beast or having a widespread intelligence network that you can use if your skilled enough in the power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T08:15:55-07:00","id":1518034,"title":"","content":"For me, Protean and the freedom it represents. Any patch of ground can be your haven for the day, you can travel in the form of an animal and perceive the night with their senses, if cornered or trapped you can become mist and escape virtually any situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T09:59:50-07:00","id":1518046,"title":"","content":"Like I mentioned before Protean is my favorite Discipline after Presence &amp; Obfuscate and will try to have that combo in later player characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T20:47:36-07:00","id":1518608,"title":"","content":"I was taken by surprise and curiosity while reading and comrpehending Protean Powers of levvels six, even, eight, and nine.<br /> <br /> Many of them have distinct concepts, ideas, occurences, states, functions, and traits related to excellence of the normal physical form of Vampires. This is of coure in addition to usual Powers that promise and reveal possible gains available in reliance on assuming, gaining, and exploring other physical, mystical, and otherworldy shapes and forms.<br /> <br /> Protean is also noted to be very convenient and efficient. Among the descriptions concpets and ideas related to beasts, verstality, darkness, and vampirism can be found. This Vampiric Discipline is also suited for combat, escapes, retreats, travel, and exploration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T23:55:01-07:00","id":1518613,"title":"","content":"Personally, I\u2019m a fan of Vicissitude, but in its less Masquerade-breachy side. Hunters got your identity pinned? Well, Obfuscate can get you out of a jam, but Vicissitude lets you have a brand new permanent face, after an hour or two of sculpting. Need to infiltrate a ghoul? Let\u2019s one-up Mission Impossible and make them an exact body-double. <br /> And, of course, if you get into combat, you just flesh-grab and <i>pull.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27967-caerolion","